{%- comment -%}
  The platform glyph for a footer link, chosen from the link's own URL.

  Matching on the URL rather than on the link's title is deliberate: the titles
  are typed in admin and are translated, so "Instagram" today could be anything
  tomorrow, while instagram.com is instagram.com in every language. It also
  means the SOCIAL column needs no special setting — a menu item pointing at a
  platform gets its mark wherever it sits, and anything else gets nothing.

  Renders nothing at all for an unrecognised URL, so a new menu item can never
  break the column.

  Accepts: url (required)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign u = url | downcase
  assign glyph = ''
  if u contains 'instagram.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-instagram'
  elsif u contains 'tiktok.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-tiktok'
  elsif u contains 'linkedin.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-linkedin'
  elsif u contains 'facebook.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-facebook'
  elsif u contains 'youtube.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-youtube'
  elsif u contains 'pinterest.com'
    assign glyph = 'icon-pinterest'
  endif
-%}
{%- if glyph != blank -%}
  <span class="wui-social-glyph" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- case glyph -%}
      {%- when 'icon-instagram' -%}{%- render 'icon-instagram' -%}
      {%- when 'icon-tiktok' -%}{%- render 'icon-tiktok' -%}
      {%- when 'icon-linkedin' -%}{%- render 'icon-linkedin' -%}
      {%- when 'icon-facebook' -%}{%- render 'icon-facebook' -%}
      {%- when 'icon-youtube' -%}{%- render 'icon-youtube' -%}
      {%- when 'icon-pinterest' -%}{%- render 'icon-pinterest' -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
